---
// Terms of use — honest draft grounded in the product's actual pilot state.
// Owner review required before the site goes live publicly.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { appUrl, siteName } from '../../lib/site.js';
---

<Base
	current=""
	title="Terms of use"
	description="Draft terms of use for the pilot service."
>
	<article class="legal">
		<h1>Terms of use</h1>
		<p class="draft-banner small">
			Draft for owner review — pending legal sign-off. This text describes
			the service as it actually behaves today.
		</p>

		<h2>1. The service</h2>
		<p>
			{siteName} is a study platform for medical exam preparation. The
			service is in active development. The live application currently
			serves a synthetic pilot examination with fixture content; no
			published clinical content pack exists yet.
		</p>

		<h2>2. Not medical advice</h2>
		<p>
			Everything in the service — questions, explanations, tutoring,
			calculators — is provided for learning. It is not medical advice,
			diagnosis, or treatment guidance, and it must not be used to make
			decisions about real patients.
		</p>

		<h2>3. Your account</h2>
		<p>
			You are responsible for your credentials and for activity under your
			account. You may be subject to a device limit and an optional
			single-active-session policy. You can delete your account from the
			application at any time.
		</p>

		<h2>4. Acceptable use</h2>
		<p>
			Do not attempt to extract, redistribute, or resell service content;
			do not interfere with other learners or with service integrity
			measures; do not upload content you have no right to use, and never
			upload patient-identifiable information.
		</p>

		<h2>5. Content and reporting</h2>
		<p>
			Questions can be reported in-app. Reported items are excluded from
			new practice pools while under review and are resolved within the
			published deadlines. Corrections are recorded as separate public
			changelog entries; your reporter notes are never published.
		</p>

		<h2>6. Payment</h2>
		<p>
			The service is free while it is in development. Paid tiers are
			planned; when payments open, the applicable prices, methods, and
			terms will be published on the pricing page before any charge can
			occur. No payment is taken today.
		</p>

		<h2>7. No warranty</h2>
		<p>
			The service is provided “as is” during development. Availability,
			features, and content may change without notice as the product moves
			through its release gates.
		</p>

		<h2>8. Governing terms</h2>
		<p>
			The operating entity, governing law, and jurisdiction will be
			specified here by the operator. Contact and dispute details will be
			published on this page when they are decided.
		</p>

		<p class="muted small">
			Questions about these terms: use the in-app reporting and feedback
			channels while the service is in development —
			<a href={appUrl}>open the app</a>.
		</p>
	</article>
</Base>
